# Form controls

Read `.cursor/rules/form-controls.mdc` before adding or restyling an input or dropdown.

Use `underlineShell`, `underlineLabel`, `underlineControl`, and `UnderlineField` from `@/components/ui/underline-field`. A field is a faint underline with the label inside it. The line turns the brand sky on focus. Text inputs, numbers, dates, textareas, and search boxes use that shell.

Use `OptionMenu` from `@/components/ui/option-menu` for a single-choice dropdown. `ClearableSelect` is that same menu. The closed control is an underline field with a chevron. The open list is a rounded panel, and the row under the pointer is the brand sky. The list is created only while the menu is open. `FieldChevron` sits in the shell when the control uses `overview-field-select`, which hides the extra chevron.

A dropdown that must accept a new typed value uses `allowCustom`, the way Section does on Settings › Fields.

Commission waterfall text inputs keep their own compact underline. Do not restyle them.

Owner Reports filters stay the multi-select, date-range, and metric controls specified in `.cursor/rules/report-requirements.mdc`. Do not replace those with `OptionMenu`. The formula editor’s suggestion list stays part of the formula field.

The spreadsheet sync policy control stays a colored status button. Its color is the policy. It is not a form dropdown.

## Checkboxes

Every checkbox uses the shared style in `app/globals.css` (base layer): a rounded box with a slate border that fills with the brand sky and a white check when checked (a white dash when indeterminate), a brand focus ring, and a dark fill in dark mode. Size it with `h-*`/`w-*` utilities if needed, but do not add border or background color utilities to a checkbox: they override the checked state.
